From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wm8960: skip the reset on boards without the codec

The SDG-8712v and SDG-8732v device trees place a wlf,wm8960 node on
i2c0, but the boards carry no WM8960. Voice runs over a SLIC, and the
mt7986-wm8960-sound machine node stays disabled. The driver still
probes, because the i2c node is present.

wm8960_i2c_probe() already tolerates a missing part in one place: it
treats a successful register read as proof that the part is not a
WM8960. A board with no part at address 0x1a passes that check,
because i2c-mt65xx returns -ENXIO on an unacknowledged transfer. The
wm8960_reset() write then fails for the same reason, and probe returns
the error.

Drop the reset write. The regmap holds wm8960_reg_defaults in a
REGCACHE_MAPLE cache, so the register view of the driver does not
change.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c |    6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wm8960.c
@@ -1485,12 +1485,6 @@ static int wm8960_i2c_probe(struct i2c_c
 		goto bulk_disable;
 	}
 
-	ret = wm8960_reset(wm8960->regmap);
-	if (ret != 0) {
-		dev_err(&i2c->dev, "Failed to issue reset\n");
-		goto bulk_disable;
-	}
-
 	if (wm8960->pdata.shared_lrclk) {
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(wm8960->regmap, WM8960_ADDCTL2,
 					 0x4, 0x4);
